ithub_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/c61bd4c97ac5a36bd1eb859c127b99e6b4f111c0","commit_subject":"Server: the status calls take turns over IPv4 and IPv6, so an access manager sees when either of a server's addresses changes (issue #802: a home server whose IP changes every few days). StatusAddressFamilyHandler, which ServerApp gives HttpAccessManager's HttpClient, sends each status on a new connection of the next family it is given (ServerApp gives IPv4 and IPv6; IPv4 alone keeps every status on IPv4, and on IPv6 only where IPv4 does not connect). A family that does not connect within 5 s gives way to the other inside the connect, before anything is sent, as a status carries usage and must never go twice; every other call keeps a pooled connection, and HttpAccessManager is unchanged. AddressFamilyConnector is the one-family connect the public-IP lookup already made, now shared by both. Tests: StatusAddressFamilyHandlerTest, against an access manager on both loopbacks at one port (TestDualStackAccessManagerServer).","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"microsoft/vscode-azureappservice","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:20:33Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b33cf5f1ff669570de04aac1396e718788dd5a8e","github_link":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-azureappservice/commit/b33cf5f1ff669570de04aac1396e718788dd5a8e","commit_subject":"Fix CodeQL registry, framing, and workflow permission findings (#2935)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"MuckRock/squarelet","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:20:24Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"58c337758db2aeabf810a860b4672ac2fa08fa8e","github_link":"https://github.com/MuckRock/squarelet/commit/58c337758db2aeabf810a860b4672ac2fa08fa8e","commit_subject":"Keep the visual seed's plans off Stripe","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"seed4j/seed4j","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:20:24Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"47ffc56c40d5be69ee5900cd60a54963feee06ab","github_link":"https://github.com/seed4j/seed4j/commit/47ffc56c40d5be